# Default settings for earlyoom. This file is sourced by /bin/sh from
# /etc/init.d/earlyoom or by systemd from earlyoom.service.

# Options to pass to earlyoom
#
# Thresholds are left at earlyoom's own defaults (10% free memory and 10%
# free swap); only the choice of victim is tuned here.
#
# This is a console-only image, so --avoid covers the processes whose death
# takes the whole session or the machine's network with it. There is nothing
# on the image that reliably eats memory the way a browser does, so no
# --prefer list is set: earlyoom falls back to picking the largest consumer,
# which is the right guess for whatever the user happened to run.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 --avoid '^(systemd|dbus-daemon|NetworkManager|sshd|login|agetty)$'"
